  receipts: [
    "**a newly enrolled witness whose honest CPU lies in (enrolment margin, per-subject line] has no standing that holds** (INVALID STATE: an identity v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin cannot admit under any disposition it offers. Undeclared, the reading is over the margin and blocks as enrolment_measured_over_margin. Declared through floor_cost_debt_typed_admissions, the live reading is at or under the line, so the admission is stale and blocks as enrolment_roster_ground_stale. HARM: the only moves left to an author are to delete the claim, to make it an ordinary function so the floor stops executing it, or to inflate its cost past the line with unrelated work. Each removes or corrupts evidence, and the first two were proposed and nearly taken on gunbc#11989. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the witness is new (the enrolment gate applies), its verdict is reached and true, and its cost is its own subject's work, not duplicated reach. A reading under the margin, or over the line with a typed admission, is not this class. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, found by review of a PR that briefly made both claims ordinary functions. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The band is a fact the gate already computes, so a general dead-band standing (self-staling on both sides, exact readings only) is decidable and expressible in the model. NEXT TRIGGER: a general repair of the dead-band policy in v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin, replacing the exact-identity authority v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_dead_band, which is the declared drop gunbc.rung_drop app_attest_verifier_enrolment_dead_band_observed_only.)",
    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#11989 (2026-09-23). test.claim.app_attest_verifier_witness_test the_key_id_step_admits_the_real_key_and_reds_on_another_key_id and the_sample_assertion_passes_rp_id_and_refuses_on_absent_extensions measured between the margin and the line on the required floor, whose required-ci-measurement-receipt names them. First they were admitted as typed cost debt, which went stale. Then they were made ordinary functions, which deleted their floor execution, and the side chat reversed that (PR comment 5795659115) in favour of an exact-two, self-staling observed-only authority.",
    "SECOND FORM, THE MARGIN STRADDLE, gunbc#12533 (2026-09-30). A dead-band row whose claim's CPU crosses the margin between runners still had no standing that holds: test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix_test a_sol_loss_mid_boot_is_reported_before_the_deadline and a_two_socket_answer_is_a_truthful_topology_refusal read 332 and 339 ms in PR floor run 36648847499, then 294 and 294 ms in run 36661418914, at identical eval_steps. Without a row the slow run refuses them over the margin; with one the fast run staled the row at the margin. The self-staling rule compared a fast runner's reading against a bound derived for a p90-slow one. REPAIR: v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin floor_enrolment_dead_band_envelope_floor applies the same measured envelope once more, and a reading in (envelope floor, margin] is EnrolmentDeadBandWithinRunnerEnvelope, typed, reported with both bounds, and not blocking; only at or under the floor is the row stale. RUNG: still mechanically preventable (a gate over a measurement), unchanged by the repair.",
    "THIRD FORM, THE LINE STRADDLE, gunbc#12800 (2026-10-01). The same spread at the per-subject line. test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix_test an_interrupted_attempts_dead_hold_is_recovered_by_the_next_one runs the real boot entry twice and read 523, 582 and 543 ms on srv1 and srv3 (PR floor runs 36765162766, 36775473983, 36783312538), then 466 ms on srv4 in merge-group run 36793281217, at comparable eval_steps. Its typed cost-debt row was right on the slow runners and stale on the fast one, a dead-band row would have been the wrong ground on the slow ones, and the stale row dequeued the change. REPAIR, the mirror of the second form's: v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin floor_enrolment_roster_envelope_floor applies the same measured envelope to the line, and a DECLARED cost-debt reading in (that floor, line] is EnrolmentRosterGroundWithinRunnerEnvelope, typed, reported with both bounds and not blocking; at or under the floor it is stale, an undeclared reading is still decided by the margin, and a dead-band row over the line is still the wrong ground.",
